correction('P001200','Inner automorphism inference','Innerness gives a representation of the orthogonal group','Innerness gives a projective representation; the spin/pin cover gives the linear representation','The scan contains no scalar-lifting argument. Implementing matrices are determined only up to scalars.','both','faithful_error')
correction('P001200','Projective diagram',r'Projective superscript appears as 12 (overwritten); \((\mathbb C^{12}\setminus0)/\mathbb C^*\)',r'If the vector space exponent is 12, its projectivization is \(\mathbb P^{11}\); retain the superscript ambiguity','Direct inspection cannot securely distinguish all retraced strokes; the dimension calculation is definite. No identification of the remaining arrows is asserted.','both','ambiguity')
correction('P001201','Theorem attribution','German Petrov-Tankin (diplomatic personal-name reading)','Retain the reading; bibliographic identification of the theorem: G. S. Petrov, 1986','The handwritten personal wording was inspected. The exact Hamiltonian, degree convention and bound match the opened original theorem by G. S. Petrov. The marginal student biography is not verified.','both','provenance')
correction('P001201','Linear-independence comment',r'A combination of \(N\) independent functions has \(N-1\) zeros',r'One can force zeros at prescribed \(N-1\) points; an upper bound requires a Chebyshev hypothesis','No inequality sign appears in the scan. The functions 1 and sin(t) on (0,10pi) disprove the unqualified exact/upper-bound reading.','both','faithful_error')
correction('P001201','Period-kernel shorthand',r'Multiply by \(H-c\) to obtain zero integral',r'This is a fixed-fiber identity; in the moving family use exact forms and multiples of \(dH\)','The text uses a fixed c. The statement is correct there but cannot be applied unchanged as the fiber parameter varies.','both','ambiguity')
correction('P001202','Pochhammer product',r'\((1;q^2)_\infty(-zq^{-1};q^2)_\infty(-z^{-1}q^{-1};q^2)_\infty\)',r'\((q^2;q^2)_\infty(-zq;q^2)_\infty(-z^{-1}q;q^2)_\infty\)','All three recorded arguments are visible. Expanding the immediately supplied zero-based definition verifies the correction; (1;q^2)_infinity is zero.','both','faithful_error')
correction('P001202','Beta odd-part inequalities','Overwritten comparisons may look non-strict','Strict decrease is required for the combinatorial interpretation; retain visual uncertainty','Each product factor contributes at most once, so the parts are distinct. This argument resolves the mathematics, not the uncertain pen strokes.','both','ambiguity')
